<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <Description>Kev decision model definitions (jaredpalmer/kev-0.8b and jaredpalmer/kev-4b, Kev 1.0) without a runtime: typed requests (one state and noul, choice and score questions, or a System One request body), Kev's request rendering and delimiter escaping in C#, the encoder that turns a request into Kev's state and question rows of token ids with the owned tokenizer (Starlings.Tokenizers profile qwen2-bpe-kev: no Microsoft.ML.Tokenizers), the checkpoints' identities and dimensions (KevModelProfile), and the decision result types. No ONNX Runtime dependency. To run the models in-process on ONNX Runtime, reference Starlings.Models.Kev.Onnx. Maturity is per model profile (Stable, Preview or Experimental): see the README, generated from the model registry.</Description>
    <PackageTags>kev;decision;classification;calibration;qwen3.5</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Starlings.Tokenizers" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- KevAnswer's constructor (the runtime builds answers from the pointer head's probabilities). -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Starlings.Models.Kev.Onnx" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Starlings.Models.Kev.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Starlings.Kev.Fidelity.Tool" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
